      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Portland annexed Multnomah on November 7, 1950, bringing city services to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multnomah%2C_Portland%2C_Oregon",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Since the 1970s, antique shops and local businesses have turned historic buildings into a vibrant pedestrian‑friendly village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multnomah%2C_Portland%2C_Oregon",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Each August, Multnomah Village hosts Multnomah Days, a parade and street festival that celebrates the community.",
